{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5 now available on AWS - AWS","context":"AWS has introduced Claude Sonnet 5, Anthropic's latest and most capable Sonnet model, which offers top-tier intelligence at Sonnet pricing for coding, agents, and everyday professional work at scale. This model delivers strong performance across various tasks, including coding, where it navigates large codebases, lands multi-file changes, and carries debugging and refactoring tasks through to completion with fewer rounds of correction. For agents, it calls tools precisely, holds state across many steps, and recovers from errors to ensure more runs finish correctly the first time. For knowledge work, it builds spreadsheets, drafts documents, and turns unstructured material into structured analysis. Customers can access Claude Sonnet 5 through two methods: Amazon Bedrock and Claude Platform on AWS. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure and provides access to Claude Sonnet 5 through a unified service with AWS-managed features like Guardrails, Knowledge Bases, and regional data residency. Claude Platform on AWS offers direct access to Anthropic's native platform experience and capabilities via the AWS Console, allowing users to build, test, and deploy with the same APIs, features, and console experience as working with Anthropic directly, unified with AWS billing and authentication","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/06/claude-sonnet-5-now-available-on-aws/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Amazon Bedrock increases default quotas for Anthropic’s Claude Sonnet 4.5 model in AWS GovCloud (US) - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock has raised the default quotas for Anthropic's Claude Sonnet 4.5 model in AWS GovCloud (US-West) and AWS GovCloud (US-East) to 5,000,000 tokens per minute and 1,000 requests per minute. This enhancement aligns the quotas with commercial AWS regions and allows for more effective scaling of AI workloads in regulated environments. Claude Sonnet 4.5 is Anthropic's latest Sonnet model, which excels at constructing complex agents, coding, and long-horizon tasks while maintaining optimal speed and cost-efficiency for high-volume use-cases. To begin using Claude Sonnet 4.5 in Amazon Bedrock, consult the News Blog, AWS GovCloud (US) console, Anthropic's Claude in Amazon Bedrock product page, and the Amazon Bedrock pricing page","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/amazon-bedrock-increases-default-sonnet-4.5-quotas-aws-govcloud-us/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Amazon Bedrock increases default quotas for Anthropic’s Claude Sonnet 4.5 model in AWS GovCloud (US) - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock, a service offered by AWS, has raised the default quotas for Anthropic's Claude Sonnet 4.5 model in AWS GovCloud (US-West) and AWS GovCloud (US-East) regions. The new quotas are set at 5,000,000 tokens per minute and 1,000 requests per minute, which is a significant 25x increase from the previous limits. This enhancement allows users to efficiently scale their AI workloads in regulated environments. Claude Sonnet 4.5 is Anthropic's latest Sonnet model, known for its proficiency in constructing intricate agents, coding, and long-term tasks while maintaining optimal speed and cost-effectiveness for high-volume applications. To begin using Claude Sonnet 4.5 in Amazon Bedrock, consult the News Blog, AWS GovCloud (US) console, Anthropic's Claude in Amazon Bedrock product page, and the Amazon Bedrock pricing page","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/amazon-bedrock-s4.5-quota-aws-govcloud-us/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"amazon-bedrock","skill_description":"Builds generative AI applications on Amazon Bedrock. Covers model invocation (Converse API, InvokeModel), RAG with Knowledge Bases, Bedrock Agents, Guardrails, and AgentCore (including the Harness managed agent loop). Applies when invoking models, setting up or migrating Knowledge Bases to Managed, deploying to AgentCore, migrating/porting/converting a Bedrock Agent (including inline agents) to an AgentCore Harness, troubleshooting Bedrock errors (ThrottlingException, AccessDeniedException), or choosing Bedrock models (Claude, Llama, Nova, Titan). Also for prompt caching, quota and throttling diagnosis, cost tracking, migrating between Claude model generations, chunking strategies, and Bedrock model selection. Covers AgentCore Payments (x402, microtransactions, Payment Manager, Connector, Instrument, Coinbase CDP, Stripe Privy, paid endpoints, agent payments). NOT for custom model training, Rekognition, or Comprehend. For SageMaker model discovery, customization, or endpoints, use aws-ai-ml.\n\nServices: bedrock, bedrock-runtime, bedrock-mantle, bedrock-agent, bedrock-agent-runtime, bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, design, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: generative-ai, rag, agents","skill_name":"amazon-bedrock"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"caching-for-llm-inference","skill_description":"Sets up a shared L2 KV cache for self-hosted LLM inference on Amazon ElastiCache for Valkey, so GPU servers load prefill KV state over EFA RDMA instead of recomputing it. Checks fit, estimates savings with KVTrace, builds a business case, creates the cache, connects vLLM or SGLang (also as NVIDIA Dynamo or llm-d workers) through an LMCache server, tunes for cost or latency, and troubleshoots. Use when a builder serves open-weight models on GPUs (for example H100 or B200, on Amazon EC2 or Amazon EKS) for multi-turn chat, agents, RAG, or long contexts and asks about KV cache offloading, prefix cache sharing, prompt caching for self-hosted models, LMCache with Valkey, or lower TTFT or GPU cost. Not for Bedrock prompt caching, LLM response or semantic caching, or general application caching.\n\nServices: elasticache, ec2\nTasks: deploy, optimize, troubleshoot\nPersona: developer, data-scientist, devops\nWorkload: ai-ml","skill_name":"caching-for-llm-inference"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search docs for Bedrock Sonnet 5 mantle pricing"}

